    "body": "<!-- pr-agent:review:full -->\n## PR Reviewer Guide 🔍\n\nHere are some key observations to aid the review process:\n\n<table>\n<tr><td>⏱️&nbsp;<strong>Estimated effort to review</strong>: 3 🔵🔵🔵⚪⚪</td></tr>\n<tr><td>🧪&nbsp;<strong>No relevant tests</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>🔒&nbsp;<strong>Security concerns</strong><br><br>\n\n<strong>Key exposure:</strong> The limiter logs the full API key on every rejected request in src/limits/bucket.ts, so keys end up in the log store.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>⚠️&nbsp;<strong>Risk level</strong>: High</td></tr>\n<tr><td>✅&nbsp;<strong>Merge recommendation</strong>: Changes required</td></tr>\n<tr><td>⚡&nbsp;<strong>Recommended focus areas for review</strong><br><br>\n\n<details><summary><a href='https://github.com/acme/acme-api/pull/101/files#diff-6f1c2a9b0e4d7a38R18-R24'><strong>Possible Issue</strong></a>\n\nThe refill reads Date.now() in milliseconds but the rate is per second, so a key refills 1000 times too fast. A test that sends 11 requests in one second to a bucket of 10 passes on this head when it should fail.\n</summary>\n\n```typescript\nconst elapsed = Date.now() - bucket.updatedAt;\nbucket.tokens = Math.min(capacity, bucket.tokens + elapsed * ratePerSecond);\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<a href='https://github.com/acme/acme-api/pull/101/files#diff-6f1c2a9b0e4d7a38R40-R44'><strong>Missed case</strong></a><br>A request without the X-API-Key header skips the limiter entirely instead of using the anonymous bucket.\n\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n"
